{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418051-the-watering-hole-water-aspected-manse","id":1418051,"title":"The Watering Hole (Water Aspected Manse)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-13T08:28:12-07:00","id":1418051,"title":"The Watering Hole (Water Aspected Manse)","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Down by the south, close to the bordermarches, a chosen of the Dragons exalted. Gaining the second breath in the distant past, he slew fair folk, cast sorcery, and created a single manse. And then he died fighting a rampaging behemoth. But the effects of his existence echoed throughout the years.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Water Hole is a manse crafted by the DB and his cronies in his final years. A Greater Manse with a Hearthstone to give control to its master. The manse has facilities for habitaiton, farming, archives, and other things which make it one of the best places to live in hundreds of miles. One of its key features is a weather control ability, as well as a sorcerous working that continuously casts 'water from stone', allowing an oasis to form in the midst of the Southern Desert heat. The manse is the last stop for guild caravans before entering the bordermarches, making it of great strategic value. It has a brisk trade with guild merchants, other nomadic tribes, and fights off the occasional fair folk incursion. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Life near the oasis is difficult, the harsh desert heat, the closeness to the Wyld, and the control over the manse giving a whole new meaning to the words 'grip on power'. Gathered around the manse, in a grouping of a thousand or more, are the descendents of the mortals the Dragonblooded once surrounded himself with.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Manse:<br /> <br /> <b>Greater Manse, water aspected, Palace Sized, constructed of Reinforced Stone</b><br /> Reduced hearthstone power<br /> Increased maintenance<br /> Geomantic Overload<br /> +4 Manse facilities<br /> 9 facilities in total<br /> <br /> Manse Facilities:<br /> Farm<br /> Workshop<br /> Wards<br /> Bound Servants<br /> Living Quarters<br /> Weather Control<br /> Barracks<br /> Fortress<br /> Artillery<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerous working: </b>Permanent Water from Stone spell. Enables non-stop production of pure, life-giving water. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Nobles</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Descended from the Dragonblooded's children, the Nobles tightly war over influence and favors, petty courtly intrigue taking over most of their lives, most of their power invested in trade with the traders and control over the manse itself. They make use of the Manse's Habitation facilities, one of the few people in the South who have access to things like Essence Lights, air conditioning, and indoor plumbing. The manse's hearthstone bearer is selected for life from them, and is capable of controlling the weather surrounding the manse, the water creation spell, who is able to enter or exit the manse via control of the automatic doors, and the bound servitors. The Nobles control the population through generous gifts, their influence over the manse, money, and the legitimacy from being descendent of the 'Great Dragon' as they call him.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">However, due to political mistakes and fading memories of the Great Dragon, their political power is waning. They know this, and are searching for ways to secure it, for failure to do so will mean death or worse. They are willing to settle for powerful artifacts, a purge of their enemies, an endorsement from a passing dragonblooded to cement their legitimacy, or in their wildest dreams, an injection of the Dragon's blood into their bloodlines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Warriors</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The manse is large, with bound servitor guardians and thick walls to protect from Fair Folk raiders and Ravagers. The populace shelters within them in the case of attack. However, the bound sevitors can only patrol within the manse itself, and staying in a fortress cooped up will only get themselves starved out. Hence the Warriors, who are enhanced by staying in the Barracks of the manse, letting them fight like Tiger Warriors with neither fear nor pity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Their leader, Black Mane, is a cunning man who wishes for more. He loves the gifts the nobles give him and his warriors... but he also knows that there is far far more in the Noble's quarters. The hearthstone bearer never leaves the manse, and is protected by guardian servitors and the Noble's personal guards, knowing that he is a weak point. Black Mane knows that he will be torn apart if he launches a coup and fails, and at best will be left stranded outside the manse to die of thirst if he loses, at worst, torn to pieces by the iron golems that patrol the manse's corridoors. He and his warriors are often watched, so it is difficult for them to pull off any sneak attacks. He will be willing to part with any amount of treasure within the manse itself if someone would help him secure command of the manse's hearthstone. With it, he shall truly become the ruler.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Crafters</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wise-Eyes in Shadow is dark haired man, rather scrawy. Known as the leader of the craftsman and the leading engineer of the people, he is one of the most knowledgeable people in the area on geomancy, crafting, and occult. He serves as a backup for the manse's maintenance requirements, ensuring that the noble-appointed sorcerer engineer has the skills needed to prevent the manse from exploding. He crafts great swords for the warriors to use, the glass pieces that assist in piercing fair folk illusion, the lenses needed to prevent blindness, and of course, the iron talismans to protect against the wyld.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">He is also ensnared by the fae. Nothing dramatic, just a simple wrong look at the wrong wyld curio. But that was enough, the intensity and potential of the wyld granting him wyld addiction and a love for the monsters within it. He is the only one so ensnared. So far he has kept this a secret. However, he has a plan. He plans to sabotage the manse defenses, using his knowledge of geomancy to shut it down. For a scant few hours, the manse will be defenseless, its guardian servitors shut down, its wards no longer functioning.<br /> <br /> Then the Fair Folk will crawl through, attacking surprised warriors, breaking through the lines, until the entire population that had taken refuge can be devoured. He wishes to make a deal with the Fair Ones; the whole settlement, for the power of the wyld. However so far he has not found anyone he can trust to get the message to the Fair Folk. Perhaps a passing amoral mercenary is willing to sell out a thousand souls? He has many great things, things which can be sold at a great price, and even more in the Noble's quarters. The entire manse turns a tidy profit each passing season. He is willing to turn over control of the manse to them, and venture into the Wyld by himself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The Guild</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This section of the southern desert has a single guild factor running it. Despite the high profits made by being able to trade with the fair folk, this is one of the few places where it is so close, and yet so stable. Most settlements near the border marhces fall to fair folk attacks, get destroyed due to natural disaster or just fail. Not this one. It is remarkably stable and safe, and is a valuable resupply station. And yet the high prices for valuable supplies often cut into profits. Well, no longer. The closest person in charge, has decided to hire out some people to wipe out the manse's inhabitants, and take control of it. The PCs can either defend it... or join in the attack, to gain the spoils.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-13-2020, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T09:58:51-07:00","id":1418061,"title":"","content":"This was made using my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407650-shantytown-of-the-awesome-building-and-manse-3e-homebrew\">manse homebrew</a>, was it not?<br /> <br /> But otherwise I like it. Useful functions, lots of interesting plot hooks, I'll probably be stealing this for my own game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T10:25:19-07:00","id":1418066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418051-the-watering-hole-water-aspected-manse?p=1418061#post1418061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was made using my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407650-shantytown-of-the-awesome-building-and-manse-3e-homebrew\">manse homebrew</a>, was it not?<br /> <br /> But otherwise I like it. Useful functions, lots of interesting plot hooks, I'll probably be stealing this for my own game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the proudest moments of homebrewing. When someone thinks that your stuff is good enough to be used. <br /> <br /> Thanks, man. And yes, it was using yours. Interesting, clever, succint... so much better than the stuff they put out in Oadenol's codex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T12:34:00-07:00","id":1418080,"title":"","content":"I like it. Very usable.<br /> <br /> Say, would you be willing to flesh-out some of the characters? Give 3-4 Intimacies to some of the main players. QC stats if you're up for it?<br /> <br /> I have a story idea for the South for my Dragon-Blooded game, will definitely be stealing this manse idea. Bit more physical description of the Manse and the story hooks would really help me out. (It's perfectly fine as-is: as a homebrew Manse that people can slot into their game and flesh out to taste this is really cool. But it's so cool, that I want more. If you're interested -- no worries if you're not.)<br /> <br /> What does the Hearthstone do? Just give control over the Manse?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Sandact6, I thought this was your system as soon as I read it. Do you have a compilation of manses made with your rules anywhere? (I'm not sure it's worth my time using your system to make manses from scratch instead of just eyeballing them -- but a big list of drag-and-drop locations would help me out.) I know there is the sample manses in the document, just wondering if there was more community stuff like this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-13-2020, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:42:08-07:00","id":1418378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418051-the-watering-hole-water-aspected-manse?p=1418080#post1418080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit more physical description of the Manse and the story hooks would really help me out. (It's perfectly fine as-is: as a homebrew Manse that people can slot into their game and flesh out to taste this is really cool. But it's so cool, that I want more. If you're interested -- no worries if you're not.)<br /> <br /> What does the Hearthstone do? Just give control over the Manse?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hearthstone does pretty much nothing. The power it had was sacrificed to add a few more facilities to the manse itself, since every single extra manse facility is vital.<br /> <br /> The Manse resembles a cross between those Chinese Mansions and European castles. There are several high spires where the artillery cannons are situated to fire on anything at the horizon and there are lookout posts, and the rest is a wide-open space spread out across the desert. The entire place is climate-controlled, with green, lots of water fountains and springs, and gardens and other things that a nobleman stuck in the middle of a desert would want to have. The thing is mostly made from a pale white marble that shines in the sun in the noon, and has over time been painted over with a large number of paintings, murals, and jewellery. There's a shitload of extra facilities inside there that aren't manse facilities, because the entire local population stays inside during Fair Folk attacks or Wyld Storms. <br /> <br /> Normally such a spread-out mansion like this would be a goddamned nightmare to patrol and protect from any form of attack, but the manse itself is well fortified, with numerous wards on top of it. There's no true limit on the number of golem guardians within it (they're stone giants of varying mass with glowing runes on them) and anyone trying to fight their way through the manse has to fight a battlegroup that is constantly regenerating, because the pieces of golems keep on putting themselves back together. It's also the reason why the manse has never been taken. Any Fair Folk that manages to punch through the deadly rain of hailstones smashing into them on the outside and has managed to punch through the wards that surround the walls (losing willpower and health levels in the process) has to fight a seemingly endless army of stone golems that do not run, do not get mind controlled, and give them zero sustenance, while the tasty minds of any mortals are far, far away like any bait. It's also built well to force attackers to get hit by ambush attacks, or funneled into choke points and bottlenecks (the guy really, really hated the Fair Folk). <br /> <br /> Inside of the manse is usually bare stone, with maybe a few benches or chairs or tables in the more public areas for seating. Think of it like a community center. In the more valuable places like the Workshops or the Living Quarters for the Nobles it gets a lot more ornate, getting things like golden statues, carpeting, fur rugs, and soft couches you see in those rich people houses. There's lots of glass, coloured and otherwise (what else are you going to use sand for). And glass windows, though some more paranoid ones choose inward-facing ones. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}